desc: Gate Keeper Low Pass Gate (4ms LPG port) by chmaha
tags: low pass gate vactrol filter vca buchla percussion
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  Vactrol-style low pass gate: a combined filter and VCA that closes with the slow, natural decay of a
  vactrol, so sounds get darker as they get quieter. In Level mode the Level knob opens the gate, like
  turning the module's knob with nothing in the Ping jack. In Ping mode every MIDI note-on strikes the
  gate, which then falls back with Decay: plucked, "bongo" sounds from any steady input.
  Color mixes in more of the unfiltered highs and slows the tail. Stereo input runs two voices, as a
  2-channel cable does on the module.
  Ported from the 4ms LPG in 4ms CoreModules (https://github.com/4ms/metamodule-core-modules, GPLv3+),
  which uses the low pass gate and envelope of Mutable Instruments Plaits by Emilie Gillet (MIT).
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code

slider1:lv_level=0.875<0,1,0.001>-Level
slider2:lv_color=0.875<0,1,0.001>-Color
slider3:lv_decay=0.875<0,1,0.001>-Decay
slider4:lv_mode=0<0,1,1{Level,Ping}>-Mode

in_pin:Left input
in_pin:Right input
out_pin:Left output
out_pin:Right output
options:no_meter

@init

ext_noinit = gfx_ext_retina = 1;
ext_nodenorm = 1;


